{
  "kanji": "相",
  "completeCard": "---\nkanji: 相\ntitle: mutual; aspect\njlpt: 3\ntags: [jlpt-n3, grade-3, structure-unclassified]\nstrokes: 9\nradical: 目\nradicalNumber: 109\nonyomi: [ソウ, ショウ]\nkunyomi: [あい-]\ndistractors: [休, 本, 目]\n---\n\n# 相 — mutual; aspect\n\n**Strokes:** 9 · **Key (radical):** 目 (no. 109) · **JLPT:** N3 (community list)\n\n## Meaning and origin\n\n相 often concerns a relation between people or things. [相談](../words/相談.md) そうだん is consultation,\nand 相手 あいて is the other party, partner, or opponent.\nThe character also has aspect and minister senses; 首相 しゅしょう means prime minister.\n\n**Modern-shape mnemonic:** imagine an eye 目 facing a tree 木, with the two sides relating to one another.\nThis is a modern association, not a verified explanation of the character's history.\n\n## Readings\n\n| Reading | Type | Typical words |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| ソウ | on | [相談](../words/相談.md) そうだん — consultation |\n| ショウ | on | 首相 しゅしょう — prime minister |\n| あい- | kun | 相手 あいて — partner; other party; opponent |\n\n## Common words\n\n- [相談](../words/相談.md) そうだん — consultation; asking for advice\n- 相手 あいて — partner; other party; opponent\n- 首相 しゅしょう — prime minister\n\n## Notes\n\n先生に相談しました。 (せんせいにそうだんしました。) — I asked my teacher for advice.\nThe mutual association does not require equal roles: a learner can consult a teacher.\n\n[休](休.md) combines a person-shaped left side with 木; 相 puts 木 on the left and 目 on the right.\n[本](本.md) has an extra stroke across 木, while [目](目.md) is only the right-hand component of 相.\n\nMetadata: [KANJIDIC2](https://www.edrdg.org/wiki/index.php/KANJIDIC_Project).\nWords: [JMdict](https://www.edrdg.org/wiki/index.php/JMdict-EDICT_Dictionary_Project), entries 1401210, 1401000, 1329300.\n",
